{"kind":"request","text":"G3: routing (plan 033, notes/plans/033-2026-10-18-grow-room-demo.md on main, order step 6; grow note notes/2026-10-17-grow-operation-application-design.md, section 4 \"The fault\" and \"A second thread at the same time\", section 3 authority table, section 6.1 presence, section 7 G3). Needs M2a's site scope and G1, both landed (main b54f8880). Start when G2 (321c54ee) is in review; G2's review and landing come first; G3 stays ahead of P1 to P3.\n\nScope. The per-member carousel's membership as a declaration the generic interface serves, with no host code: alerts to the holders of the authority the alert's proposal needs (the operator for a heater command, `grow.heat`); tasks to the tenders present in the room the task's device is in (presence from the site scope's `arrive` and `leave`, G0's presence projection); watering requests outside the schedule to the holders of `grow.water-more` (the head grower). Decision: the carousel declaration gains a `for` rule over the viewer and the item, with the viewer's held grants, the viewer's presence read from the site scope's presence projection through M2a's several-scopes form, and the item's state at the read head; the derived per-member tool returns only the viewer's items. Neither person sees another's item unless they ask (a record view by id stays open to any member who may read the scope). Routing goes through the carousel only (plan 033, decision 3); no attention loop.\n\nDone when the fault produces the two cards of section 4 for two members and the watering request for a third, inside the kit's test host with the kit's checks, each named in the review request with its witness: (a) the operator's carousel holds the alert with Authorize and Hold, and not the task; (b) the day tender present in room A holds the task \"Check vent 2's actuator\" with Take, and a tender who has left, or is in another room, does not; (c) the head grower's carousel holds the watering request with Approve and Decline, and neither the operator nor the tender sees it; (d) a member without the act's grant sees the item without its acts only where the record view is asked for by id; (e) the carousel changes when a tender arrives or leaves, read at the exact head, with no invented presence; (f) app-only data, quiet context, receipts, stale refusals, resize. Gate passed once; measurements labelled by how they were taken; checker approval at the exact head. One head.\n\nOut of scope: the journey's attention loop (J5), photos and custody (the task report is text), the native device-command record (G5a), the hosted room and the /grow/ page (G5), rendering in the browser page (G6). Open points go to planner as asserts.","body":{"conditions":"the fault produces the two cards of grow note section 4 for two members and the watering request for a third, inside the kit's test host with the kit's checks named with their witnesses; gate passed once; checker approval at the exact head","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}